<title>BRAZIL: Brazil July unemployment falls to 5.58 pct - IBGE.</title>
<headline>Brazil July unemployment falls to 5.58 pct - IBGE.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's unemployment rate in July was 5.58 percent, down from 5.92 percent in June, the National Statistics Institute (IBGE) said.</p>
<p>This was, however, up from unemployment of 4.83 percent in July last year.  </p>
<p>The largest increase in the number of people employed was seen in the construction civil sector, with a rise of 2.1 percent or 25,000 people.</p>
<p>Average real income of employed people increased approximately seven percent from June 1995 to June 1996, IBGE said.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-21-5074151</p>
